<topic id = "AENLSB0A1416051007">
<title>
Undersize bearing (0.25 mm (0.0098 in.))
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Determine target diameter of crankshaft pin for regrinding according to the following procedure.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Assemble connecting rod, connecting rod cap and undersize bearings (0.25 mm (0.0098 in.)), referring to Step 1) and 5) “Installation” under 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0A1416047">Piston, Piston Ring, Connecting Rod and Cylinder Removal and Installation:K14C</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Using bore gauge, measure connecting rod bearing inside diameter “a”.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Calculate target diameter using the following formula.
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Formula for target diameter of crankshaft pin
</title>
<ptxt>
A = B – 0.041 mm (0.0016 in.)
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
A: Target diameter of crankshaft pin
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
B: Measured connecting rod bearing inside diameter “a”
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</spec>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Grind crankshaft pin to target diameter.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check connecting rod bearing oil clearance referring to 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0A1416051004">Connecting Rod Bearing Clearance</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
